      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-08-19_WidnesExaminer_art0052" n="art0052">
        <head>MAKING NEW LODGES.</head>
        <p>MAKING NEW LODGES.</p>
        <p>A new lodge, called "The Pride of the Hill," con- nected with the local district of the National United Free Gardeners. was opened at the Tiger Vaults, Brownlow-hill. Liverpool, on saturday. About ao members and friends were invited to supper by the host, /dr.Thomas I,luyd. Afterwards the lodge was opened in dile course by the district officers from Warrington, Bros. Jamsa Rudge; D.M. ; Thomas Coggen, ; Councillor James Hill, district secretary ; and officers from the Liverpool lodges. On Monday evening a new lodge of the same dis- trict was opened at the house of Mr. Samuel May, the Mariner's Hotel, Percival-lane, Runcorn, called the " Pride of Runcorn." by the district officers, Bro. James nudge, D. 1.; Time, Coggen, D.D.M., of Liverpool ; Thomas Daly, D.T., of Warrington; Councillor James Hill, district secretary ; John Budge, D. trustee, and Bros. Dyer and May, of the Pride of Liverpool Lodge. After the opening, at which 20 new members were made, Bros. Budge, j Daly, and Coggen fully explained the objects of the ' o:der, and the benefits to be secured by joining it.</p>
      </div>
