nedy • l6 J Settle B Taberner J Morris l2 W Gargins 2l J Poulding 2l Moses Cotton WII Gorrell R llough 2l T Yates Total 215 Total 204 Majority, 11 for Wigan. KILLED BY WASPS. * In France, as in England, there is a plague of wasps. owing to the exceptional and long-continued heat of this summer. A gentleman named Carre,residing at Chfilons- sur-Marne, was out in his garden trying to destroy a wasp's nest, when he was attacked by a large swarm and severely stung all over the face and head. He ran indoors in a pitiable state, and sent for a doctor. But it was too late The unfortunate gentleman was dead be- fore relief could be obtained for him. There have been several similar cases during the last month, and less eerious injuries by wasps are extremely frequent. 1 .I. The Medical Annual advises .Practitioners to remember that when recommending Cocoas as food and beverage for invalids, the name CADBURY on any packet of Cocoa is a gu irantee cii purity.—Adot. The Lancashire County Justices on Wednesday inflicted a penalty of £lOO and costs upon a publican at Eccles nanied Frederick Greenwood for using his house as a place for betting. RUPTURE CURED.—S. J. SHERMAN, Hernia Specialist. 64, Chancery-lane, London, sends his book on rupture post free. Brauch Chambers, 26, King-st., Manchester. —Advt.</p>
