        <p>WARRINGTON HIGHWAY BOARD. The quarterly meeting of the above Board was held in the Surveyor's Office, Sankey-st., on Wed- nesday, when there were present Captain T. E. Withington (chairman), Messrs. James Houghton, James Millington, John Grounds, Joseph Clare, T. Lowe, Henry Bate, and J. Kerfoot, H. B. White (clerk), A. White (deputy clerk), and T. Thompsm (surveyor).—The SURVEYOR, reported that he had inter- viewed Mr. Thomas Tunstall of the Brookside House, as to the proposed straightening of the road at Elalton's Bridge, Penketh. Mr. Tunstall objected to any land being taken as it would entail removal of trees which he greatly prized.—Mr. MILLINGTON said that they could not do anything until they could get the consent of the land ow ner.—The SURVEYOR said that he would approach Mr. Tunstall again before the next meeting of the Board in November.—The CLERK: When the leaves are off the trees perhaps he would not value them so much.—The Finance Committee's minutes which showed that several townships had not paid in their accounts, were passed on the motion of Mr. Houghton, seconded by Mi. Kerfoot.</p>
